item.description:
SQLite &quot;INSERT OR REPLACE INTO&quot; vs. &quot;UPDATE &hellip; WHERE&quot; SQLite &ldquo;INSERT OR REPLACE INTO&rdquo; vs. &ldquo;UPDATE &hellip; WHERE&rdquo;
When performing operations on a database, there are many ways to approach a given task. In this article, we will look at the differences between the SQLite commands INSERT OR REPLACE INTO and UPDATE ... WHERE.
What is the Difference? The UPDATE ... WHERE command will only update a row if it already exists.
